  <running_head>INSTITUTOINUM</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">voluntate fidera constant. Alioquin</l>
    <l n="2">enim ipsis competeret ea quoque felici-</l>
    <l n="3">tas, quæ intellectui &amp; voluntati debe-</l>
    <l n="4">tur. At id videtur Sacris literis repu-</l>
    <l n="5">gnare. Deinde animæ sensitivæ pariter</l>
    <l n="6">nulla indicia sunt. Nam quæ de visu &amp;</l>
    <l n="7">auditu astrorum quidam referunt, profu-</l>
    <l n="8">sus confidta videntur. Denique animæ</l>
    <l n="9">vegetativæ operationes etiam non no-</l>
    <l n="10">tamus, quia fidera nec nutriri, nec au-</l>
    <l n="11">gmentari, nec generare advertuntur.</l>
    <l n="12">Imo aliam speciem astris attribuere</l>
    <l n="13">deberemus, quam nunc quiquam astris</l>
    <l n="14">adjudicant.</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">§. 4. Quarta quæstio fit: <i>An qua-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>quam ratione astris anima tribui possit?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">Plato &amp; alii recentiores quidam Phi-</l>
    <l n="18">losophi agnoscunt posse astris animam</l>
    <l n="19">aliquam tribui, non quatenus ea su-</l>
    <l n="20">mitur pro peculiari aliqua animæ spe-</l>
    <l n="21">cie, nempe vegetativa, sensitiva vel ra-</l>
    <l n="22">tionali: sed quatenus ea sumitur pro</l>
    <l n="23">virtute quadam <i>συνεργητική</i> communi, &amp;</l>
    <l n="24">cognoscente, materialiter tamen. In</l>
    <l n="25">hanc sententiam venerunt 1. quia ob-</l>
    <l n="26">servarunt talem motus constantiam &amp;</l>
    <l n="27">varietatem, quam sine cognoscente</l>
    <l n="28">principio expediri non posse arbitran-</l>
    <l n="29">tur. 2. quia perfectio fiderum major,</l>
    <l n="30">quam aliorum corporum, solo homine</l>
    <l n="31">excepto,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek word "συνεργητική" approximated; uncertain. Page lacks catchword and signature.</notes>
